## ngrok agent config — backend tunnel only.
##
## Why only the backend goes through ngrok: free tier allocates one public URL
## per agent at a time (account-level limit; v2/v3 yaml format doesn't
## change it). The backend gets the reserved free static domain so
## NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL stays stable across restarts (Next.js bakes it at
## compile time).
##
## The frontend is exposed via Cloudflare quick tunnels (cloudflared) instead
## — see run.sh. trycloudflare.com URLs are random per restart but invisible
## to phones because the QR uses window.location.origin.
##
## This file is the SHAPE of the config. It is NOT consumed directly because
## ngrok yaml does not interpolate env vars. `./run.sh --tunnel` reads your
## env (NGROK_AUTHTOKEN, NGROK_BACKEND_DOMAIN) and writes the real config to
## `.ngrok.yml` (gitignored) before launching ngrok.
##
## One-time setup:
##   1. ngrok signup → https://dashboard.ngrok.com (free).
##   2. Copy your authtoken from the ngrok dashboard.
##   3. Reserve one static domain (free tier allows 1) for the backend.
##   4. Add to backend/.env (or your shell):
##        NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=2abc...
##        NGROK_BACKEND_DOMAIN=fifth-morphine-shock.ngrok-free.dev
##   5. brew install cloudflared
##   6. ./run.sh --tunnel

version: "2"
authtoken: ${NGROK_AUTHTOKEN}
tunnels:
  backend:
    proto: http
    addr: 8000
    domain: ${NGROK_BACKEND_DOMAIN}
